WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.520
Let's get right into audience questions&nbsp;
for this week. First one is interesting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:07.520
relates to a thing, to a few different things&nbsp;
we've talked about over the last few years. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:13.280
the question is, what is the most likely&nbsp;
future of socialism in the United States?&nbsp;

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:18.560
If you watched the recent State of the Union&nbsp;
addresses from Donald Trump, you would know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:25.600
that this powerful, defiant declaration that&nbsp;
the U.S. will never be a socialist country&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:31.360
is both an impossible prediction to make, because&nbsp;
the truth is, we're terrible at predicting things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:36.640
even five years out. Who knows what the U.S.&nbsp;
could look like 20, 30, 50, 100 years out.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:42.320
But it's also particularly its meaninglessly&nbsp;
propagandistic in the sense that there's no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:48.560
threat that the U.S. is about to become socialist,&nbsp;
despite Donald Trump continuing to campaign on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:55.760
Biden's been taken over by the Socialists. The&nbsp;
people Trump claims are controlling Biden aren't,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:02.000
by and large, actual socialists. And certainly&nbsp;
there's nothing socialistic about Joe Biden's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.640
policy. So the fear mongering about the U.S.&nbsp;
becoming socialist is very, very silly, but it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:11.920
does seem to at least activate some of the people&nbsp;
on the right. But I think those people are mostly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:19.040
supporting Donald Trump anyway. I think it's&nbsp;
essentially a wash. So then we get to a Trump free&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:23.920
discussion of the possible future of socialism&nbsp;
in the United States, as I have said before.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:29.760
I have seen no evidence that if the U.S. is to&nbsp;
become a socialist country and again, this is not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:34.800
about my views. I'm not a socialist. I'm a social&nbsp;
Democrat, which is a form of highly regulated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:40.560
capitalism. If the country is to become socialist,&nbsp;
I believe that you would need to see first of all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:48.240
actual socialists have some amount of power in the&nbsp;
United States. Now, this could be socialist groups&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:54.400
or socialist politicians. Right now I don't see&nbsp;
either. And I believe it would be incremental. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.400 --> 00:02:00.720
would go through social democracy. Acceleration&nbsp;
ism is the idea when applied to socialism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:09.040
capitalism, that by accelerating capitalism,&nbsp;
which some socialists believe will fail.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:16.560
Some Marxist, some communists believe will fail.&nbsp;
You accelerate the eventual revolution that will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:23.120
turn the country socialistic. Much has been said&nbsp;
theoretically about that and written theoretically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:28.080
about that. I believe that in practice at this&nbsp;
point in time, again, in five years, maybe I'd&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:34.080
have a different view because things dramatically&nbsp;
change right now. I don't see how, for example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:39.920
giving Trump another four years and cutting&nbsp;
regulations and giving more market power.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:46.720
I don't think that if that causes a breakdown, it&nbsp;
results in the United States becoming socialist.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:51.760
If and so this is why I've said time and again to&nbsp;
actual socialists, of which there are relatively&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:56.400
few in the United States. Many of the people&nbsp;
who even think they are socialists aren't really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:02.720
socialists. Up for now, you should just be joining&nbsp;
the fight for social democracy because the path&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:10.960
to let me put it a different way. The best proof&nbsp;
that the United States should go in that direction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:17.200
would be to go in that direction. And that would&nbsp;
mean looking at health care more like northern&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:22.160
European countries. Look at it, looking at&nbsp;
taxation more the way northern European countries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:30.160
look at it, look at education, social welfare&nbsp;
programs, etc.. In the last decade, we have seen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:37.200
socialists go from really more of an insult and&nbsp;
not something many people would use to describe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:42.480
themselves to kind of like a pretty ho hum.&nbsp;
You know, it's just a word. It's almost become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:47.200
like progressive, although it means very different&nbsp;
things where Trump says all his opponents are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:53.280
socialists. Very few people really believe&nbsp;
it. Young people are more okay with the term&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:59.280
than we've seen people be in a very long time. So&nbsp;
I think that and it's not for me to give advice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:05.520
to the actual socialists not being one, but if you&nbsp;
are an actual socialist, you should capitalize on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:10.800
the most positive or least negative view of&nbsp;
socialism that there has been in the U.S. in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:18.000
a long time by pushing the country in any&nbsp;
ways that are possible in that direction.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:25.360
The best argument you can make for socialism being&nbsp;
great would be for social democracy to work really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:30.800
well. And if we ever got to that point, then I&nbsp;
and the Socialists would be on different sides.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:35.920
But but right now, even though many of the&nbsp;
socialists believe they're on a different side&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:41.440
than me, the next step, whether you want social&nbsp;
democracy, is the end point or you want socialism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:50.160
as the endpoint would be to move in that direction&nbsp;
when it comes to all of the major areas of policy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:54.320
in the United States. It's certainly not going to&nbsp;
happen with another four years of Donald Trump.

